.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt PDPCONTROL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pdpcontrol
.Nd control the PiDP-10 engine
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar subcommand
.Op Ar argument
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
starts, stops and inspects the PDP-10 engine.
The engine is the system unit
.Ar pidp10-engine@boot Ns No \&.service ,
which runs simh as the
.Nm pidp10
user inside a detached
.Xr screen 1
session named
.Dq pidp10 .
That session is where simh's
.Ic sim>
prompt is; the telnet port
.Pq Ev PIDP10_CONSOLE_PORT
is the PDP-10's own terminal.
.Pp
Members of the
.Nm pidp10
group can start and stop the engine units without a password (a polkit
rule) and attach to the session (a
.Xr sudoers 5
rule).
Add yourself with
.Ic sudo usermod -aG pidp10 Ns No \ \& Ns Ar you
and log in again.
.Pp
Subcommands:
.Bl -tag -width restart
.It Cm start Op Ar boot
Boot a system.
.Ar boot
is the octal switch-register value the maintenance panel would be set to
(1 boots ITS, 2 TOPS-10 on the stock selections file); it becomes the unit's
instance.
With no
.Ar boot
the instance is
.Dq default :
.Ev PIDP10_BOOT ,
or the panel switches when a front panel is attached.
Which system directory a number boots is decided by
.Pa /var/lib/pidp10/systems/selections
(the directory is
.Ev PIDP10_SYSTEMS ,
defaulting to
.Pa /var/lib/pidp10/systems ;
it lives in the state tree because the boot scripts and the disk images they
attach are one directory).
A running engine with another boot number is stopped first: there is one
cabinet.
.It Cm stop
Polite stop: the unit's
.Nm pidp10-stop
types ^E and
.Ic quit
into the session, so simh flushes its disk buffers.
This is a power switch, not an operating-system shutdown: bring ITS down
from the console first.
.It Cm restart Op Ar boot
Stop, then start.
.It Cm status
Which units are active.
.It Cm stat
Console port, state directories and active units.
.It Cm console Op Cm pdp6
Attach to the simh session of the PDP-10, or of the PDP-6
.Pq Pa pidp10-pdp6.service ,
in this terminal.
^E stops the machine at
.Ic sim> ,
.Ic c
continues, Ctrl-A d detaches.
.It Cm halt Op Cm pdp6
Stop the CPU at
.Ic sim>
without stopping the engine: types ^E into the session.
Attach and type
.Ic c
to continue.
.El
.Pp
Operator policy is read from
.Pa /etc/pidp10/pidp10.conf
(the same file the units load), so
.Ev PIDP10_BOOT ,
.Ev PIDP10_PANEL
and
.Ev PIDP10_CONSOLE_PORT
set there apply here too.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/log/pidp10/pidp10-console.log , /var/log/pidp10/pidp6-console.log
Everything the sessions printed.
.It Pa /etc/sudoers.d/pidp10
Who may attach.
.It Pa /usr/share/polkit-1/rules.d/50-pidp10.rules
Who may start and stop the units.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic pdpcontrol start 1
Boot ITS.
.It Ic pdpcontrol console
Get to
.Ic sim> .
.It Ic pdpcontrol stop
Stop whatever is running, flushing disks.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pdp 1 ,
.Xr screen 1 ,
.Xr systemctl 1 ,
.Pa /usr/share/doc/pidp10/README.md
